# The YTsaurus monorepo, present only for its `.proto` files: `ytsaurus-proto`
# generates its bindings straight from `third_party/ytsaurus/yt/yt_proto/`
# rather than from a copy, so the protocol definitions cannot silently drift
# from upstream's.
#
# A submodule records an exact commit, which is what the pinning rule asks for.
# Do NOT init it with a bare `git submodule update --init`: that checks out the
# whole monorepo. Use `./scripts/init-protos.sh`, which clones it shallow and
# sparse — 23 MB instead of the whole tree.
[submodule "ytsaurus"]
	path = third_party/ytsaurus
	url = https://github.com/ytsaurus/ytsaurus.git
	branch = stable/25.4
	shallow = true
